UNIT carried_canonical
LANG ts
PRIMARY-SHA256 f0f8bfd7fcf65ee10da915c5044801760095bf39afc82f9b18fe04a03e3cf1a3
SIG export default function carried_canonical(table: { [key: string]: Json }): string
ABI TypeScript compiles to the js runtime and is driven exactly as js. The artifact declares
  `type Json = null | boolean | number | string | Json[] | { [key: string]: Json }`; map = that index-signature object
  (an own "__proto__" key is an ordinary own property); none = null; text = string; f64 = number; list = Array. Every
  throw (R6) is an Error. STRICT: the artifact type-checks under `strict: true` with no `any`, no non-null assertions
  (`!`), no `@ts-ignore` and no `@ts-expect-error`. It is an ES module default-exporting the function and imports nothing.
ENVELOPE as the primary: the js widening (non-map tables, undefined, holes, host objects) is not typed here and stays OUT.
MECHANISM (restated from js; language files are self-contained) a recursive writer over Json, never JSON.stringify on a
  container and never a rebuilt object (own-key enumeration hoists array-index keys and would undo R2). Scalars:
  JSON.stringify for string/boolean/null; a number throws unless Number.isFinite(x) && !Object.is(x, -0), else
  JSON.stringify(x). Arrays in order. Maps: Object.keys(x).sort() with the default comparator (UTF-16 code units, R2).
  Narrow with typeof, Array.isArray and null checks; no casts.
DEPENDS-ON none
PROVENANCE rederive@b15b56613f9d cli/sir/v05.mjs `canonical` and `plainMap`. Language file re-cut 2026-10-26 with the primary.
